>>
endobj
301 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 232 0 R
/E (This project focuses on developing a Digital Twin framework for a 5-DOF robotic arm. The system combines a physical robotic arm fabricated using 3D-printed components with a virtual model created in Unity. The digital twin enables visualization and interaction with the robotic arm in a simulated environment, providing a platform for testing and analysis without affecting the physical hardware.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
302 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 232 0 R
/T (2. Project Significance)
/E (2. Project Significance)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
303 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 232 0 R
/E (The project demonstrates the application of Digital Twin technology in robotics and automation. By integrating simulation, embedded systems, and machine learning, the system provides a cost-effective solution for operator training, robotic system monitoring, virtual testing, and educational research. The developed platform can be extended for future industrial and smart manufacturing applications.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
304 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 232 0 R
/E (Motivation )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
305 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1523 0 R
/E (With the rapid advancement of Industry 4.0 technologies, there is an increasing demand for intelligent systems that can improve efficiency, safety, and productivity in industrial environments. Traditional robotic systems often require extensive physical testing, which can be time-consuming, costly, and prone to operational risks. Digital Twin technology offers a promising solution by creating a virtual representation of a physical system, enabling real-time monitoring, simulation, and analysis.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
306 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1524 0 R
/E (The motivation behind this project is to explore the integration of robotics, simulation, and artificial intelligence through the development of a Digital Twin-based robotic arm. By creating a synchronized virtual model of a physical robotic arm, users can visualize operations, test different scenarios, and analyze system behavior without affecting the actual hardware. This approach reduces development time, minimizes potential damage to equipment, and provides a safe environment for experimentation and training.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
307 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1525 0 R
/E (Furthermore, the project aims to provide a cost-effective learning and research platform for understanding modern concepts such as Digital Twins, machine learning, embedded systems, and robotic control. The knowledge gained from this project can contribute to future applications in industrial automation, remote monitoring, smart manufacturing, and intelligent robotic systems.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
