422 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1594 0 R
/E (The NodeMCU \(ESP8266\) is used in the project to provide wireless communication and IoT connectivity for the robotic arm. It enables the system to connect to a Wi-Fi network and exchange data between the physical robotic arm and the Digital Twin environment.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
423 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1595 0 R
/E (The NodeMCU receives control commands from the user interface and transmits them to the Arduino UNO for robotic arm operation. It also supports remote monitoring and control through IoT platforms, allowing users to interact with the robotic arm from any location. Its built-in Wi-Fi capability, compact size, and low cost make it an ideal choice for implementing wireless communication in the project.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
