429 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1600 0 R
/E (In this project, SG90 servos are responsible for controlling the base, shoulder, elbow, wrist, and gripper movements of the 5-DOF robotic arm. The servos receive PWM \(Pulse Width Modulation\) signals from the Arduino UNO, allowing accurate positioning of each joint. Due to their low cost, ease of interfacing, and adequate torque for lightweight payloads, SG90 servo motors were selected as an effective solution for the robotic arm system)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
430 0 obj
<<
