446 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 244 0 R
/T (Blender was used to assemble and visualize the 3D components of the robotic arm in a virtual environment before physical fabrication. The imported STL files of individual parts were positioned, aligned, rotated, and assembled to create the complete robotic arm model. Using Blender helped verify the proper fit and orientation of the components, identify assembly issues, and ensure that the overall structure was correctly formed before integration into the Digital Twin environment. This reduced design errors and provided a clear visualization of the final robotic arm assembly.)
/E (Blender was used to assemble and visualize the 3D components of the robotic arm in a virtual environment before physical fabrication. The imported STL files of individual parts were positioned, aligned, rotated, and assembled to create the complete robotic arm model. Using Blender helped verify the proper fit and orientation of the components, identify assembly issues, and ensure that the overall structure was correctly formed before integration into the Digital Twin environment. This reduced design errors and provided a clear visualization of the final robotic arm assembly.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
