448 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 244 0 R
/T (The Arduino Integrated Development Environment \(IDE\) is the software platform used for writing, compiling, and uploading programs to the Arduino UNO microcontroller. It provides a user-friendly interface that simplifies the development and testing of embedded applications. In this project, Arduino IDE was used to develop the control program for the robotic arm, enabling the operation of SG90 servo motors and communication between the Arduino UNO and NodeMCU modules. The software facilitated code development, debugging, and real-time testing, ensuring reliable control of the robotic arm system.)
/E (The Arduino Integrated Development Environment \(IDE\) is the software platform used for writing, compiling, and uploading programs to the Arduino UNO microcontroller. It provides a user-friendly interface that simplifies the development and testing of embedded applications. In this project, Arduino IDE was used to develop the control program for the robotic arm, enabling the operation of SG90 servo motors and communication between the Arduino UNO and NodeMCU modules. The software facilitated code development, debugging, and real-time testing, ensuring reliable control of the robotic arm system.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
