473 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 246 0 R
/E (The Internet of Things \(IoT\) is a technology that enables physical devices to connect to the internet, allowing them to exchange data and be monitored or controlled remotely. IoT integrates sensors, microcontrollers, communication modules, and cloud platforms to create intelligent systems that can be accessed from anywhere using a smartphone, tablet, or computer.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
474 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 246 0 R
/E (In this project, IoT is implemented using the ESP8266 \(NodeMCU\) microcontroller, which provides built-in Wi-Fi connectivity. The NodeMCU acts as a bridge between the robotic arm and the internet, enabling users to control the arm wirelessly through a web interface and the Blynk mobile application. Commands sent from the user interface are transmitted over Wi-Fi to the ESP8266, which then controls the servo motors to perform the desired movements.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
