/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1699 0 R
/E (Blynk is an Internet of Things \(IoT\) platform that enables users to remotely monitor and control hardware devices through a smartphone application. It provides an easy-to-use interface for developing IoT projects without requiring extensive knowledge of mobile application development. The platform consists of three main components: the Blynk mobile application, the Blynk Cloud server, and the hardware device \(ESP8266 NodeMCU\).)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
620 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1700 0 R
/E (In this project, the Blynk platform is used to control the robotic arm wirelessly. The ESP8266 \(NodeMCU\) connects to the internet via Wi-Fi and communicates with the Blynk Cloud. Commands sent from the Blynk mobile application are received by the ESP8266, which then controls the servo motors to perform the required movements.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
