685 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 258 0 R
/E (Machine Learning \(ML\) was incorporated into the robotic arm system to predict the appropriate joint angles for a desired end-effector position. Instead of manually calculating inverse kinematics every time, a neural network model was trained using a dataset generated through forward kinematics. The complete process consists of dataset generation, data preprocessing, model training, performance evaluation, and prediction.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
686 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 258 0 R
/T (Step 1: Dataset Generation Using Python)
/E (Step 1: Dataset Generation Using Python)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
687 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 258 0 R
/E (The first step is to generate a large dataset that represents different configurations of the robotic arm. Since collecting thousands of real-world measurements is time-consuming, a Python program was developed to generate synthetic data using forward kinematics equations.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
