696 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1757 0 R
/E (The generated dataset contains 100,000 samples, which are sufficient for training the machine learning model.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
697 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 258 0 R
/E (Dataset generation is one of the most important stages in the development of the intelligent robotic arm because it provides the data required to train and evaluate the machine learning model. In this project, the dataset consists of robotic arm joint angles, end-effector positions \(X, Y, and Z coordinates\), and torque values generated using forward kinematics. A large number of samples were created to represent different arm configurations and movements within the robot's workspace.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
698 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 258 0 R
/E (The generated dataset enables the machine learning model to learn the relationship between the end-effector position and the corresponding joint angles. As a result, the trained model can accurately predict the required servo motor angles for a desired target position, reducing computational complexity compared to solving inverse kinematics repeatedly.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
699 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 258 0 R
/E (A well-generated dataset improves the accuracy, reliability, and generalization capability of the machine learning model. It forms the foundation of the digital twin by enabling intelligent prediction, real-time simulation, and synchronization between the physical robotic arm and its virtual counterpart. Therefore, dataset generation plays a crucial role in achieving the objectives of Industry 4.0 by integrating robotics, artificial intelligence, and digital twin technology into a single intelligent system.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
