/P 265 0 R
/T (Torque estimation is an important aspect of robotic arm design because it determines the amount of rotational force required by each servo motor to lift a given payload. Instead of manually calculating torque for every robotic arm configuration, a machine learning model was developed to predict the torque required at each joint. The complete process includes dataset generation, preprocessing, model training, evaluation, and prediction.)
/E (Torque estimation is an important aspect of robotic arm design because it determines the amount of rotational force required by each servo motor to lift a given payload. Instead of manually calculating torque for every robotic arm configuration, a machine learning model was developed to predict the torque required at each joint. The complete process includes dataset generation, preprocessing, model training, evaluation, and prediction.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [3]
>>
