988 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 270 0 R
/E (After completing the assembly of all robotic arm components in Blender, the entire model was exported in the FBX \(Filmbox\) format. The FBX format was chosen because it preserves the 3D geometry, object hierarchy, pivot points, transformations, and material information during the export process. The exported FBX file was then imported into Unity, where it served as the digital twin of the physical robotic arm. This ensured that the model maintained its structural integrity and allowed individual joints to be controlled accurately during simulation and real-time operation.)
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
989 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1859 0 R
/E (To achieve realistic movement, individual joints were linked according to the kinematic structure of the robotic arm. C# scripts were developed and attached to the corresponding joints, allowing each servo motor angle received from the ESP8266 to control the rotation of its digital counterpart. This enabled real-time synchronization between the physical robotic arm and its virtual model.)
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
