998 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 271 0 R
/T (After importing the robotic arm model into Unity, the virtual model was synchronized with the physical robotic arm using the ESP8266 \(NodeMCU\) and the Blynk IoT platform. The NodeMCU continuously transmitted the real-time servo motor angles over Wi-Fi through Blynk. Unity received these angle values and applied them to the corresponding joints of the virtual robotic arm. As a result, every movement performed by the physical robotic arm was simultaneously reflected in the Unity environment, creating a real-time digital twin. This synchronization enabled accurate visualization, monitoring, and control of the robotic arm within the virtual environment.)
/E (After importing the robotic arm model into Unity, the virtual model was synchronized with the physical robotic arm using the ESP8266 \(NodeMCU\) and the Blynk IoT platform. The NodeMCU continuously transmitted the real-time servo motor angles over Wi-Fi through Blynk. Unity received these angle values and applied them to the corresponding joints of the virtual robotic arm. As a result, every movement performed by the physical robotic arm was simultaneously reflected in the Unity environment, creating a real-time digital twin. This synchronization enabled accurate visualization, monitoring, and control of the robotic arm within the virtual environment.)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
