/E (This project successfully developed a Digital Twin-based 5-DOF robotic arm capable of real-time synchronization between the physical robot and its virtual counterpart. The robotic arm was designed using CAD models, fabricated through 3D printing, assembled, and controlled using servo motors interfaced with an ESP8266-based IoT system.)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1081 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1883 0 R
/E (A virtual replica of the robotic arm was created in Unity using Blender-generated 3D models. Real-time communication between the physical robot and the Digital Twin was achieved through Wi-Fi using the Blynk platform, enabling remote monitoring and control.)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1082 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1884 0 R
/E (Machine Learning techniques were implemented using TensorFlow to predict robotic joint movements from the generated dataset, improving the intelligence of the system and demonstrating the potential for data-driven robotic control. The integration of the Meta Quest VR headset further enhanced user interaction by providing an immersive virtual training environment.)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1083 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1885 0 R
/E (The project successfully combines Robotics, IoT, Machine Learning, Digital Twin technology, and Virtual Reality into a single Industry 4.0 framework. The developed system offers a cost-effective, scalable, and educational platform suitable for industrial automation, remote operation, operator training, and future research. Overall, the project demonstrates the practical implementation of modern smart manufacturing concepts and highlights the significant role of Digital Twin technology in the next generation of intelligent robotic systems.)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
